        "title": "Visit this only if you're a Hindu and religious",
        "text": "The temple is in bad condition owing to the improper management and poor habits of most devotees visiting this place.\nThe main Shivling is kept open only in mornings and evenings between 5.30 - 7.30 PM. I visited in afternoon around 2.30 and was disappointed as the ShivLing was closed. Visiting this temple is considered very important in the Hindu community and hence I had to visit this temple again in the evening just to get a glimpse of the ShivLing.\nThere's a ghat just behind the main temple where bodies are cremated openly, so stay away from the smoke.\nThere are monkeys, lambs, goats, dogs all over the premises.\nThe shoe counter can get full and you'll have to keep the shoes outside at your own risk (Not to worry i guess). \nThere's also a pigeon feeding place in the premises.",
