        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r487184894-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Mixed feelings",
        "text": "People told me about the big aarti ceremony they have in evening. So I went to catch this aarti ceremony. Heard it starts at sharp 7:00, but strangely that day it started late by almost 40 minute. \n\nThere are two aarti which goes on simultaneously. One in the temple and outside across the ghat. The setup of the outside one is strange enough. Right below is a holy river, where people come for hindu ceremony before cremation is done. So one side there were people coming for this process and one place there is aarti going on. You kinda get a mixed feeling, and that too vibe is very strong.\n\nOne more strange rule - white skin is not allowed in the premises of temple.",
