      {
        "review_id": 486700197,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r486700197-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Needs more maintenance",
        "text": "Much talked about from outside Nepal as prime attraction.  But the maintenance is poor.  Bagmathi rever on the rear looks pathetic.  Non Hindus cannot access inside temple though they are charged NPR1000 as entry fee.  No footware, phone, camera inside temple campus.  Storage facility for footware, camera and phone are available but may be crowded sometime to make the deposit.  It is good to make photos etc before depositing and leave them in your car (not on unknown taxies) with the driver acknowledging it.  Hundered of domes with hindu deities but no information displays around.  Pasu Pathi Nath.  Pasu (Globe) Pathy (the leader /cammander) Nath (dwelling place).  Hindu religion believes Brahma is the creator of the lives on earth, Vishnu is the protector of the lives and Shive (Pasupathy) is the destroyer of lives once their time on earth is completed.  Even today deadbodies are cremaated on the banks of Bhagmati river at the rear of Pasupathynath temple with the belief departed souls will reach heaven direclty abode of Shiva.  It may rain time and hence good to have an umbrella ",
